                <p class="card-link-copy">On EU servers in Germany, with infrastructure provided by Hetzner, under GDPR-aligned practice. Your crews work from anywhere over WhatsApp, while the record itself sits on European infrastructure rather than on personal phones and paper.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Does EU hosting suit New Zealand?</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">As general information, New Zealand's privacy regime sets expectations around holding personal information, including overseas. GDPR-aligned EU hosting gives a documented basis for where data sits. Confirm your own obligations; we share details on request.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Why not just keep paper?</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">A structured digital record is searchable, time-stamped and machine-readable, with each photo and fault status against the right item. Paper gets lost and is hard to produce on demand. A PDF exports from the digital record whenever you need one.</p>
